2025-11-27 14:00:42,929 - app.llm.services - DEBUG - [REQUESTS] Request body: b'{"model": "llama3.2:latest", "prompt": "You are analyzing news articles for a Scottish heritage and culture newsletter with a primarily US-Scots diaspora audience - people of Scottish descent living in the United States, Canada, Australia, and other countries who maintain an interest in the history and culture of their \\"old country\\".\\n\\nImagine a typical reader: someone of Scottish descent living in the US, with family connections to Scotland, interested in learning about the \\"old country\\" - its history, culture, traditions, and contemporary developments that matter.\\n\\nArticle Title: Oil and gas heavyweight highlights North Sea decommissioning cost burden\\nURL: https://www.heraldscotland.com/news/25651505.energean-profits-fall-amid-security-fears-off-israel/?ref=rss\\n\\nArticle Content (first 2000 chars):\\nBusinessEconomyFinanceIndustryPolitics Oil and gasheavyweight Energean has racked up hefty bills associated with a reduction in UKNorth Seaactivity as it underlined the risks facing its core operations inIsrael. London-listed Energean incurred $36 million (\\u00a320m) decommissioning costs in respect of the Wenlock and Tors fields in the North Sea in the latest period during which operations in Israel were disrupted amid the conflict inGaza. Energean noted that production from the key Karish and Karish North fields was suspended for 12 days in June. This came after Israel\\u2019s energy and infrastructure ministry ordered the suspension of operations on the Energean Power floating production storage and offloading (FPSO) vessel, which handles the output from the fields. Accounts for the Energean Israel venture note: \\u201cSince 7 October 2023, the magnitude of regional geopolitical risk has been elevated. Concerns of escalation in the Middle East have intensified the security risk in the region, as essential infrastructure systems (such as the Energean Power FPSO offshore Israel) may be targets for missile fire and sabotage operations.\\u201d The accounts add: \\u201cAny event that impacts production from the Karish and Karish North fields could have a material adverse impact on the business, results of operations, cash flows, financial condition and prospects of the Group.\\u201d Read more However, the accounts note that production from Karish and Karish North has continued without interruption since the suspension in June. They highlight the fact that the Israeli Government announced a ceasefire in respect of the conflict in Gaza in October. Energean\\u2019s chief executive Mathios Rigas said: \\u201cDespite the challenging geopolitical and macro environment, our business remained resilient.\\u201d Energean made $828 million underlying profit before tax in the nine months to September 30, compared with $894m in the same period last time. The company noted the fall in profits reflected factors such as \\u201cthe Ministry o\\n\\nYour task:\\n1. Rate this article on FIVE separate dimensions, each on a scale of 1-100. CRITICAL: Most stories should have MOST dimensions scoring 10-40. Only truly exceptional stories should have dimensions above 70. Be CRITICAL and use LOW scores liberally.\\n\\n   HISTORICAL INTEREST (1-100): \\n   - Scores 1-20: No historical content, just current events\\n   - Scores 21-40: Minor historical mention or local history\\n   - Scores 41-60: Some historical context\\n   - Scores 61-80: Substantial historical content, heritage sites, notable historical figures\\n   - Scores 81-100: Major historical discoveries, archaeology, preservation of national heritage\\n\\n   CULTURAL INTEREST (1-100):\\n   - Scores 1-20: No cultural content, just daily news\\n   - Scores 21-40: Minor cultural mention\\n   - Scores 41-60: Some cultural context\\n   - Scores 61-80: Substantial cultural content (traditions, language, arts)\\n   - Scores 81-100: Major cultural significance, festivals, cultural revivals\\n\\n   QUIRKY IN